# 98 DECLARES NOTHING AT ALL, and it is a THIRD KIND of empty declaration.  Phase 92's
# was code that COULD NOT RUN -- readfile() was already unreachable.  Phase 96's was a
# POSSIBILITY THAT HAD NEVER EXISTED -- neither `FILE *` had been opened in any build.
# This one is an EQUALITY.  The code it replaces runs constantly: `towupper` alone is
# entered 892 times in a trivial session, from `utf_islower()` inside
# `buf_init_chartab()`, BEFORE 'casemap' has been applied and with arguments in exactly
# 128..255.  What is claimed is that eleven libc functions and six <ctype.h> macros
# have been replaced by C that computes the same answer.
#
# SO THE EVIDENCE IS EQUIVALENCE, NOT UNREACHABILITY, and phase/098/check.sh says
# what it is.  tools/muslcase.py re-derives all 1,114,112 codepoints from THIS
# MACHINE'S libc through ctypes and compares them with the 187 + 171 convertStruct rows
# the phase shipped; tools/muslctype.py slices the seventeen functions OUT OF THE
# PRODUCED SOURCE, compiles them with -Wall -Wextra and runs them beside libc's over
# 1,002,140 int values, 137,560 atoi/atol strings and 1,845 bsearch lookups compared by
# POINTER.  Both are proven able to fail.
#
# AND THE CORPUS CANNOT SEE ANY OF IT, which is why fourteen probe sessions run on both
# binaries beside the recording.  Every one of the 102 screen cases seeds itself by
# TYPING ASCII, so nothing in it reaches Unicode case folding, 'casemap', the four
# bsearch tables or the sort.  The probes do: six over an ASCII, a Latin-1, a Greek, a
# Cyrillic, a circled Latin and a Coptic letter under every 'casemap' the option can
# hold -- the first three separate an ASCII fallback and the last two separate vim's
# own table, and a text with only one group would pass one of the two wrong answers --
# four for the four bsearch tables, three for atoi and atol, one for the chartab those
# 892 startup calls build, and :undolist read out of the RAW STREAM, because the
# Press-ENTER redraw wipes it before the \x1b[?25h that ends a step.
#
# Measured: two full recordings, the binary the phase was handed against the one it
# made, are byte-identical -- all 102 screen cases, all 111 Ex-command rows, all 30
# command lines, the four pty scenarios and the nineteen terminal rows -- and
# tools/zerodelta.sh --phase 98 finds the same against whim-vim's frozen baselines.
#
